<Project>

  <!--
    Shipped in the package's build/ folder, so it is imported into every consuming project.

    Surfaces <RedisMinServerVersion> to the analyzer. An analyzer cannot see the server you will connect to, so
    version-gated suggestions (SER301 and friends) are shown by default; set this and you only get the ones your
    server can actually run:

      <PropertyGroup>
        <RedisMinServerVersion>7.4</RedisMinServerVersion>
      </PropertyGroup>

    The equivalent .editorconfig / .globalconfig spelling is `redis.min_server_version`, which takes precedence.
    Major.minor is what is read; anything more precise is accepted and ignored.

    CompilerVisibleProperty is what makes the property readable at all - without it the analyzer simply never
    sees the value. The property is surfaced under its own name rather than being copied to some internal one:
    this file is imported *before* the consuming project's own PropertyGroup, so anything we read here at
    evaluation time is still empty. The item declaration is safe because the value is read later, at compile
    time, by which point the consumer's setting is in effect.

    It reaches the analyzer as `build_property.RedisMinServerVersion`.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <CompilerVisibleProperty Include="RedisMinServerVersion" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
